WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.930
The Netherlands, 1995.

2
00:00:02.980 --> 00:00:08.250
The rivers are high, just two
years after the high water of 1993.

3
00:00:08.300 --> 00:00:12.530
More than 250,000 residents
have to leave their homes.

4
00:00:12.580 --> 00:00:15.500
The planners take a
design flow for the Rhine:

5
00:00:15.550 --> 00:00:20.030
16,000 cubic metres a second at
Lobith, on the German border.

6
00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.910
The answer was not simply higher dikes.

7
00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.250
So what did they do?

8
00:00:24.300 --> 00:00:26.430
One giant dam on the Rhine?

9
00:00:26.480 --> 00:00:27.750
Move everyone out?

10
00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:31.010
In this mission, you'll test
flood forecasts and warnings,

11
00:00:31.060 --> 00:00:34.810
and why planners use
ranges, not single numbers.

12
00:00:34.860 --> 00:00:37.370
Then you'll compare China's
response on the Yangtze,

13
00:00:37.420 --> 00:00:43.250
after the country's 1998 floods
affected 186 million people.

14
00:00:43.300 --> 00:00:46.170
Your mission: find out
how the Dutch responded,

15
00:00:46.220 --> 00:00:48.350
if not simply with higher dikes.
